{
  "$comment": [
    "Command registry. Phrases are matched after normalization: lowercase, number words -> digits, filler words (the, a, to, please, can, you, ...) removed — so write phrases naturally, fillers are ignored on both sides.",
    "Phrase syntax: (a|b) = alternatives, [word] = optional, {slot} = parameter defined under 'slots'. Entries are tried top to bottom and the first exact match wins, so keep specific phrases above general ones.",
    "cms.body: a value that is exactly \"{slot}\" (or \"{a|b}\" = first of a, b that was spoken) is replaced by the slot's typed value; if the slot wasn't spoken, cms.fallbacks names a config 'defaults' key to use instead (a real CMS name you configure); if still missing, cms.ask is spoken and nothing is executed. Unfilled optional fields are dropped.",
    "Every cms.endpoint is a route under apps/api's /api/voice-control (lights, ac, volume, door, screen, content). The API resolves spoken names against the real devices/screens/content and answers with real names on errors. Volume goes to the TV's IR remote (the soundbar follows it); the remote is one-way, so there is no absolute volume and no level is ever reported.",
    "Slot types: number (min/max, out of range = no match), enum (canonical value -> spoken aliases), text (a name, passed to the CMS as spoken with numbers as digits; 'anchor' = must start or end with one of those words, e.g. \"screen 2\" / \"lobby screen\"). The CMS resolves names — never put real device/screen names in phrases.",
    "rewrites: spoken forms Vosk produces, rewritten before matching (it spells letters out: \"AC\" -> \"a c\").",
    "reply may contain {timeGreeting}: Good morning / afternoon / evening for the current Indian Standard Time.",
    "Aliases: slots 'light' and 'screenAlias' map the names people say to the real CMS names. Free-text name slots with aliasesFrom are also translated when the whole name is an alias (e.g. \"play intro on tusker 27\")."
  ],
  "rewrites": {
    "a c": "ac",
    "air con": "ac",
    "t v": "tv"
  },
  "slots": {
    "brightness": {
      "type": "number",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100
    },
    "temperature": {
      "type": "number",
      "min": 16,
      "max": 30
    },
    "steps": {
      "type": "number",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 10
    },
    "volume": {
      "type": "number",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100
    },
    "color": {
      "type": "enum",
      "values": {
        "red": [
          "red"
        ],
        "green": [
          "green"
        ],
        "blue": [
          "blue"
        ],
        "white": [
          "white"
        ],
        "warm white": [
          "warm white",
          "warm"
        ],
        "cool white": [
          "cool white",
          "cold white",
          "cool",
          "cold"
        ],
        "yellow": [
          "yellow"
        ],
        "orange": [
          "orange"
        ],
        "purple": [
          "purple",
          "violet"
        ],
        "pink": [
          "pink"
        ],
        "cyan": [
          "cyan"
        ]
      }
    },
    "mode": {
      "type": "enum",
      "values": {
        "cool": [
          "cool",
          "cooling",
          "cold"
        ],
        "heat": [
          "heat",
          "heating",
          "hot",
          "warm"
        ],
        "auto": [
          "auto",
          "automatic"
        ],
        "fan": [
          "fan",
          "fan only"
        ],
        "dry": [
          "dry",
          "dehumidify"
        ]
      }
    },
    "target": {
      "type": "text",
      "aliasesFrom": "light"
    },
    "screen": {
      "type": "text",
      "aliasesFrom": "screenAlias"
    },
    "content": {
      "type": "text"
    },
    "namedScreen": {
      "type": "text",
      "anchor": [
        "screen",
        "display"
      ],
      "aliasesFrom": "screenAlias"
    },
    "light": {
      "type": "enum",
      "values": {
        "Strip Light": [
          "tusker edge"
        ],
        "Stretch Fabric 0": [
          "tusker l 1",
          "tusker el 1",
          "tusker l1"
        ],
        "Stretch Fabric 1": [
          "tusker l 2",
          "tusker el 2",
          "tusker l2"
        ],
        "Stretch Fabric": [
          "tusker l 3",
          "tusker el 3",
          "tusker l3"
        ]
      }
    },
    "screenAlias": {
      "type": "enum",
      "values": {
        "tv 86 inch": [
          "tusker 86"
        ],
        "screen 2": [
          "tusker 27"
        ]
      }
    }
  },
